{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC6 drafted and pushed for review: Gerrit change 2549 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2549\n\nAdds `infra/runbooks/gerrit-host-wedged-ssm-lost.md` (232 lines): symptom, a six-check confirmation list separating this failure from an impaired instance, the shell-free snapshot -> modify-volume -> reboot recovery, verification, the deferred measurement step, and the mandatory follow-up. It leads with the UNWEDGE-not-a-fix framing as its own READ FIRST section, carrying the 29-GiB-before/29-GiB-after denominator argument, so 'grew the volume' cannot be recorded as a resolution.\n\nCorrectness check worth noting: the draft cited `vol-0270fcf13709cf472` as the root volume, which could not be confirmed from Terraform (the root device is created implicitly by `root_block_device` in main.tf, so the id lives only in AWS state) — and the DATA volume `vol-06fa2e77a9dd97527` is the one hardcoded in the other runbooks, so the two are easy to confuse in a document that tells an operator which volume to grow. Verified against the live API before pushing: `describe-instances` reports RootDeviceName `/dev/xvda` mapped to `vol-0270fcf13709cf472`, with `vol-06fa2e77a9dd97527` on `/dev/sdf`. The runbook names the correct volume.\n\nTwo incidental findings while drafting:\n\n1. `root_volume_size_gb` in infra/terraform/variables.tf is ALREADY 60 — commit 3e22693efc90 ('infra: codify 60 GiB root volume') landed the 30->60 codification, so the out-of-band modify-volume is reconciled and the daily drift check should be green on that axis.\n\n2. Because `rebar-root-disk-pressure` is now `breaching`, a truncated series SHOULD page. The runbook says that if the series truncates and no page arrives, check the SNS subscription before trusting the silence — worth chasing on the epic if it ever happens.\n\nRemaining on this bug after 2549 lands: AC1's induced-publish-stop verification and AC2's replay of the recorded series against the new configuration. Both are live-AWS verification steps rather than code."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788400775779732001,"uuid":"27daa3b1-d2d7-4059-95bd-a03380ffbb8e"}